# (build 132c) The lost music part the owner hears on the Mega Drive, most
# often after pausing and unpausing -- the ROM's own, kept. The pause jingle
# turns the music down (cfE8_MusPause, the walk: $FF - volume onto each part
# in use); the only thing that turns it back up is the unpause jingle's FM5
# track, which ends its phrase, about 30 ticks long, with the unpause
# command (E8 00). An effect on FM5 started inside that window -- 51 of the
# 56 effects, the selection sound A plays among them -- takes the track over
# and the walk never runs: each part stays down until its next instrument or
# volume change, in a looping song often never. Motavia: pause, unpause,
# A three ticks later; music tracks 1-3 left turned down (`expect stuck`,
# the high byte). From about 27 ticks on the walk has run (stuck_hunt.py).

start slot 1 routes/saves/jet_scooter.json
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait screen level
wait idle
wait ticks 30
press start
wait ticks 40
press start
wait ticks 3
press a
wait ticks 150
expect stuck $0E00          # music tracks 1-3 down, none lent
